          "text": "     1→# use-ai Monorepo\n     2→\n     3→A TypeScript monorepo using Bun for building AI-powered React applications with WebSocket-based AI agent integration.\n     4→\n     5→## Structure\n     6→\n     7→```\n     8→.\n     9→├── packages/\n    10→│   ├── client/          # @use-ai/client - React hooks library for AI integrations\n    11→│   └── server/          # @use-ai/server - WebSocket server for AI agent hosting\n    12→└── apps/\n    13→    └── example/         # Example AI-powered todo list app\n    14→```\n    15→\n    16→## Getting Started\n    17→\n    18→### Install Dependencies\n    19→\n    20→```bash\n    21→bun install\n    22→```\n    23→\n    24→### Development\n    25→\n    26→1. Start the AI server (requires `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` environment variable):\n    27→```bash\n    28→export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_api_key_here\n    29→bun run start:server\n    30→```\n    31→\n    32→The server will start on port 8080.\n    33→\n    34→2. In another terminal, run the example app:\n    35→```bash\n    36→bun run dev\n    37→```\n    38→\n    39→This will start a dev server at http://localhost:3000\n    40→\n    41→### Logging\n    42→\n    43→The server supports two logging formats controlled by the `LOG_FORMAT` environment variable:\n    44→\n    45→#### Pretty Logging (Default - Development)\n    46→Human-readable logs with emojis and formatting:\n    47→```bash\n    48→export LOG_FORMAT=pretty\n    49→bun run start:server\n    50→```\n    51→\n    52→Output example:\n    53→```\n    54→━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n    55→📤 API REQUEST\n    56→━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n    57→🔧 TOOLS: addTodo, deleteTodo, toggleTodo\n    58→💬 MESSAGES: 3 total\n    59→  1. [user] add a todo for groceries\n    60→  2. [assistant] 2 content blocks\n    61→  3. [user] 2 content blocks\n    62→━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n    63→```\n    64→\n    65→#### JSON Logging (Production)\n    66→Structured JSON logs for parsing by tools like Datadog, CloudWatch, etc.:\n    67→```bash\n    68→export LOG_FORMAT=json\n    69→bun run start:server\n    70→```\n    71→\n    72→Output example:\n    73→```json\n    74→{\"timestamp\":\"2025-01-06T10:30:45.123Z\",\"level\":\"info\",\"message\":\"API request\",\"tools\":[\"addTodo\",\"deleteTodo\"],\"messageCount\":3}\n    75→{\"timestamp\":\"2025-01-06T10:30:45.456Z\",\"level\":\"info\",\"message\":\"Tool calls\",\"toolCount\":1,\"tools\":[{\"name\":\"addTodo\",\"input\":{\"text\":\"groceries\"}}]}\n    76→```\n    77→\n    78→### Build\n    79→\n    80→Build all packages:\n    81→```bash\n    82→bun run build\n    83→```\n    84→\n    85→Build individual packages:\n    86→```bash\n    87→bun run build:client\n    88→bun run build:server\n    89→```\n    90→\n    91→### Testing\n    92→\n    93→#### Unit Tests\n    94→Run all unit tests across the monorepo:\n    95→```bash\n    96→bun test\n    97→```\n    98→\n    99→#### E2E Tests\n   100→End-to-end tests using Playwright with real Claude API calls:\n   101→\n   102→```bash\n   103→# Run E2E tests (requires ANTHROPIC_API_KEY)\n   104→export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_api_key_here\n   105→bun run test:e2e\n   106→\n   107→# Run with UI mode (interactive)\n   108→bun run test:e2e:ui\n   109→\n   110→# Run with headed browser (visible)\n   111→bun run test:e2e:headed\n   112→\n   113→# Run in debug mode\n   114→bun run test:e2e:debug\n   115→```\n   116→\n   117→E2E tests are located in `apps/example/test/` and test real interactions with the AI including edge cases like deleting non-existent items.\n   118→\n   119→## Packages\n   120→\n   121→### @use-ai/client\n   122→\n   123→React hooks library for AI integrations using WebMCP (Model Context Protocol). Features:\n   124→- `UseAIProvider` context component for WebSocket connection configuration\n   125→- Built-in floating AI chat UI (optional) - just enable with `showFloatingChat={true}`\n   126→- `useAI` hook that accepts tool definitions for AI agent function calling\n   127→- Automatic tool execution and result streaming\n   128→- Beautiful, responsive chat interface with message history\n   129→\n   130→### @use-ai/server\n   131→\n   132→WebSocket server that hosts AI agents and proxies requests to Claude API. Features:\n   133→- WebSocket-based client communication\n   134→- MCP tool registration and execution\n   135→- Conversation history management\n   136→- Claude API integration\n   137→- Dual-mode logging (pretty for development, JSON for production)\n   138→\n   139→### example\n   140→\n   141→An AI-powered todo list application demonstrating the use-ai library. The AI can:\n   142→- Add, delete, and toggle todos via natural language\n   143→- Query the current todo list\n   144→- Understand context and perform multiple operations\n   145→\n   146→## Tech Stack\n   147→\n   148→- **Runtime**: Bun\n   149→- **Language**: TypeScript\n   150→- **UI Framework**: React\n   151→- **AI Model**: Claude (Anthropic)\n   152→- **Protocol**: WebSocket + WebMCP\n   153→- **Build Tool**: Bun bundler\n   154→\n   155→## Usage Examples\n   156→\n   157→### Floating AI Chat (Recommended)\n   158→\n   159→The easiest way to add AI capabilities is using the built-in floating chat UI:\n   160→\n   161→```tsx\n   162→import { UseAIProvider } from '@use-ai/client';\n   163→import App from './App';\n   164→import { todoTools } from './tools';\n   165→\n   166→<UseAIProvider\n   167→  serverUrl=\"ws://localhost:8080\"\n   168→  showFloatingChat={true}\n   169→  globalTools={todoTools}\n   170→>\n   171→  <App />\n   172→</UseAIProvider>\n   173→```\n   174→\n   175→This displays a floating \"AI\" button in the bottom-right corner. Users can click it to open a chat interface and interact with your app using natural language.\n   176→\n   177→### Programmatic API\n   178→\n   179→For custom UI implementations:\n   180→\n   181→```tsx\n   182→import { UseAIProvider, useAI } from '@use-ai/client';\n   183→\n   184→function App() {\n   185→  const { response, loading, generate } = useAI({\n   186→    tools: {\n   187→      addTodo: {\n   188→        fn: (input) => addTodo(input.text),\n   189→        config: {\n   190→          description: 'Add a new todo item',\n   191→          parameters: {\n   192→            text: { type: 'string', required: true }\n   193→          }\n   194→        }\n   195→      }\n   196→    }\n   197→  });\n   198→\n   199→  return (\n   200→    <div>\n   201→      <button onClick={() => generate('Add a todo for grocery shopping')}>\n   202→        Ask AI\n   203→      </button>\n   204→      {response && <p>{response}</p>}\n   205→    </div>\n   206→  );\n   207→}\n   208→\n   209→<UseAIProvider serverUrl=\"ws://localhost:8080\">\n   210→  <App />\n   211→</UseAIProvider>\n   212→```\n   213→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n",
